{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1483116-assassin-s-creed-in-tc-assasins","id":1483116,"title":"Assassin's Creed in TC Assasins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-05T03:32:06-07:00","id":1483116,"title":"Assassin's Creed in TC Assasins","content":"How would you recreate some Assassin's Creed games elements in TC Assassins' game?<br /> <br /> With <b><i>Daughters of Jacobins</i></b> being 'modern Assassins Order' and <b><i>Society of Leonidas</i></b> being sorta Templars - it's still leave a whole swaths of timelines to propagate.<br /> <br /> I think that series of Societies that resemble AC Assassins Order across time is good path? Like frist pre1000s Assassins being <a href=\"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Hidden_Ones?\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Hidden Ones</i></b></a>. <a href=\"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Masyaf\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Masyaf Assassins</i></b></a> in 1000s being second - and probably <b><a href=\"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Italian_Brotherhood_of_Assassins\" target=\"_blank\">Renaissance Europe group</a></b> ( Italy mainly ) being third. Then in 1800s we got modern <b><i>Daughters of Jacobins</i></b> as legacy of those, with Italian Brotherhood being disbanded in 1750s in Italy's unification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-21-2023, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T13:02:57-07:00","id":1483330,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how &quot;Assassins Creed-like&quot; it would be, but a sourcebook that looked at playing TC:Assassins in different specific historical settings - Rennaissance Milan/Italian city states, Cold War Berlin, 18th century Ottoman Empire, Japanese Shogunate, Reign of Terror Paris, Tudor or Stuart England, Prohibition Chicago, ancient Rome, classic Cyberpunk - would be a lot of fun. Each one would probably have some alterations to some existing factions and new ones totally unique to each setting, as well as period specific equipment, abilities and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T23:20:24-07:00","id":1483848,"title":"","content":"Well, the unification of the Kingdom of Italy actually happened in 1861.<br /> In 1815 <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Austria gained Venice</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and much of northern Italy according to the Congress of Vienna and (more or less) in this period we had the Carbonari (</span></span></span>lit.<span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">'charcoal makers'): </span></span></span>an informal network of secret revolutionary societies active in Italy from about 1800 to 1831.<br /> Although their goals often had a patriotic and liberal basis, they lacked a clear immediate political agenda. They were a focus for those unhappy with the repressive political situation in Italy following 1815, especially in the south of the Italian Peninsula. Members of the Carbonari, and those influenced by them, took part in important events in the process of Italian unification (called the Risorgimento), especially the failed Revolution of 1820, and in the further development of Italian nationalism. The chief purpose was to defeat tyranny and to establish a constitutional government. In the north of Italy other groups, such as the Adelfia and the Filadelfia, were associate organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27462-william-wilson","name":"William Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T19:44:10-07:00","id":1490579,"title":"","content":"<b>Notice - we use here extensively Assassin's Creed setting</b>, to not reinvent things for Trinity Continuum alone. We SHOULD probably create new Societies based on those concepts - but let's assume that AC names are short hands for TC final groups. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> Having playing <b>AC Origins</b> extensively lately and re-reading <b>TC Assassins</b>, I see this like this...<br /> <br /> At the start of everything ( probably in <b>TC Aegis</b> era) comes to being <b> Order of Ancients</b> - tyrannical plotters of Bronze and Iron Era, using alien artifacts of various cosmic races falling on Earth from <b>Trinity Continuum</b>. Order was overusing power and authority, assassinating often noble in heart man and women that disagree with it's values...<br /> <br /> In 490s BC future King of Kings of Persian Empire - <b>Xerxes the Great</b> - joins <i>Order of Ancient</i> and in few years is the first open ruler supported by the conspiracy. He is killed in 465 BC by freedom fighters that quickly became <b><a href=\"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Hidden_Ones\" target=\"_blank\"> Hidden Ones</a></b>, secret brotherhood dedicated at stopping the Order and defending common people. ( Events of <b>AC Odyssey </b>) <i>Hidden Ones</i> will be mentioned later as predecessors of <b><i>Daughters of Jacobins</i></b> in coming centuries...<br /> <br /> <i>Hidden Ones</i> will be fighting next centuries with <i>Order of Ancients</i>, themselves become more and more organised. By circa 48 BC they are order-like themselves, re-shaped by intrigues of Rome, Egypt and Greece around Cleopatra and Cesar - created stable Creed in those years - and by popular belief in Anubis and other Death Gods of the era... ( Events of <b>AC Origins </b>)<br /> <br /> By around 900 CE polytheistic cults that <i>Order of the Ancients</i> often infiltrated are dying in Abrahamic Europe. Society reforms into <i><b> Order of Solomon's Temple </b></i> - commonly known as <i>Knights Templars</i>. ( Events of <b>AC Valhalla </b>) They evoke various religious wars and conflicts - and by 1119 they grew so vain - they publicly announce they existence, in times of Crusades. Shadow parts of organisation are very dissatisfied by this move but support general Orders goals. For now...<br /> <br /> <i>Templars</i> in Holy Land are fighting with <i>Hidden Ones</i> Islamic successors - <b> Hashashims</b> , working from fortress Almud in Masyaf. ( Events of <b>AC 1 </b>) Simplified in English to <b><i>Order of Assassins</i></b>, they survived up to late 1300s, clashing with Templars all the time. Then both Societies seemingly ended before 15th century, Shadows breathed with a relief. ( Events of <b>AC</b> 1 and it's spin-offs ) Not for long...<br /> <br /> Fall of Constantinople in 1453 CE brought art and science bloom to Europe, known as Renaissance. Like the era name, it bring the Rebirth of two greatest sides of conflict - <b><i>Brotherhood of Assassins</i></b> and creation of <i><b>Society of Leonidas</b> </i>in Italy, Later Society was continuator of Knights Templars traditions...<br /> <br /> Both groups clashed often till the end of Assassins as we know it - till French Revolution. Assassins Order backed the Jacobins, and later, Great Terror of that era. Confronted with negation of the values \u200b\u200bthey professed, Assassins finally disbanded in inner civil war over the ideas of Revolution. In their death of organisation, <i>Daughters of Jacobins</i> were born, passing the Creed for new generations till this very day... \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-21-2023, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}